WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know our first guest
tonight from his work

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:03.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
on "Saturday Night Live," wher
he serves as a head writer

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.338 size:75% position:38%
as well as co-anchor
of "Weekend Update."

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
He stars in
"Tom &amp; Jerry: The Movie,"

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.010
which premieres in theater
and on HBO Max on Friday.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:14.014
Please welcome back to the sho
our very good friend Colin Jost.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:15.782 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you, buddy?

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Great. How are you?
-Good.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.019 line:92%
It's so wonderful to see you

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
I cannot believe --
-I started waving --

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you introduced Raghav
I started waving.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:24.557 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Just I was like,

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:26.292
"Maybe he thinks I'm pretty good
at drumming."

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"See where this goes."

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:34.267
-Yeah, a lot of people have said
you're a 16-year-old drummer

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.502 line:92%
who's taken the world by storm

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:38.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I was like,
"Well, I mean, I'll take it.

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:42.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know I read as late teens,
but...

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:45.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys are doing
your fifth show in a row.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:48.681 size:84% position:42%
I believe your last run
was six shows in a row.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:51.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
That is a very punishing
schedule.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, a lot of it
is necessitated

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:55.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
by the times
we're living through,

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:58.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
but are you --
you must be exhausted.

00:00:58.158 --> 00:01:00.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, mentally,
I think a lot of us

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:02.695 line:92%
are hitting a breaking point

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:06.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's very hard --
it's extremely hard to complai

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:07.600 line:92%
when you work at a comedy show

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
Be like, "We worked
five weeks in a row!"

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:13.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, to any --
You understand,

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:17.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
but to any sort of, you know
normal functioning human,

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:18.945 size:84% position:42% line:92%
they're like, "Uh-huh."

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:20.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
you can't, like, complain.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:22.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
With my parents, I'm like,
"Yeah, Mom, you know,

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:25.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can't believe I'm workin
five weeks in a row."

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:29.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she's like, "Yeah, I worke
just in, like, hospitals

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:32.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
for like six years straigh
without a week off.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, no,
that must be tough."

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're like, "Yeah,
okay, that's harder."

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:38.364
-That does make sense, 'caus
I've been trying to get people

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:41.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
to bang pots and pans
at the end of each "SNL"

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:43.770 line:92%
just to, like, reward you guys

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it hasn't taken off
in the same way?

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:49.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, nobody wants to engag
that, but I will say --

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:51.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think if you were
thinking of it as booing

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:54.380
and they're booing along, yo
might get some people to join.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.016
Certain weeks, you might
get some people to join in

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Some people said
they would like

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.687 line:92%
to come out on their balconies

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:03.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
and just scream how
it was better in the '70s.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:06.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
Yeah, that's right.

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.128 align:start size:94% position:6%
They didn't do enough
with the host.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:11.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
Cast is great.
Writers are terrible.

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:12.532 size:75% position:38% line:92%
They just yell that.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:16.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, I mean,
a very real cost of this -

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:17.170 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and obviously, again,

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is the right choice
based on safety --

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:22.175
but, you know, whether the "SNL"
was good or bad,

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:24.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
the nicest part of the way
the week was structured

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:28.214
is at the end of the show,
you went out with everybody.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it could either
lift your mood

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:33.987 align:start size:94% position:6%
or, if your mood was great
it would elevate it.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:37.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
So how weird is it
when the shows are over

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:40.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
that everybody
just kind of dissipates?

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:40.860 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's very strange.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:44.164
I mean, the first part is,
there's no energy backstage.

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:47.167
So when you get off, if yo
felt like things went grea

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:51.204
or you felt they went horribly
either way, there's nothing.

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.206 size:75% position:38%
You walk into, like,
a wall of silence.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.241 size:75% position:38%
Normally, you'd see,
you know, whatever.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.211
Adam Levine's there, and he'
like, "Hey, what's up, man

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.112 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Good job."

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:01.214 line:92%
Or, you know, there's a llam

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Abraham Lincoln
from the costume before.

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
the Abraham Lincoln's,

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:06.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, got a couple notes
for you --

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.254 line:92%
"Maybe hold your head this way,"

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
or whatever, you know,
things like that.

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.357 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You're getting energy.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:12.625 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And this is --

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:13.993 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You have no --

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have nothing.
And then there's no --

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
Normally, you would
sort of decompress

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:18.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
with your friends
after the show,

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:21.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, like, your fello
castmates, the writers.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
You'd talk about
how things went.

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:27.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then you're operating
in this weird vacuum

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.541 line:92%
and you have none of the release

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:30.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
and none of the social par
of the show.

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:33.780
And there's no -- It must be
so weird to start this year,

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, new people that started,
because there's no, like,

00:03:37.317 --> 00:03:39.419 size:78% position:39%
going out for a drink
after the table read

00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:43.456
and learning about why thing
aren't getting in the show

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:44.757 line:92%
or not getting in the show

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everyone's living
in their own weird vacuum.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when you see people
with masks on,

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:52.765
you never want to talk
to anyone with a mask on.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're just like,
"Yeah, alright, whatever."

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:57.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
It feels like you're greetin
someone in a hospital.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.072 line:92%
-It's so true about new people

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:00.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I remember
when I started,

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.342 line:92%
one of my first reactions was,

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Huh, so there's no cocain
anymore."

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:08.414
And now for them, it must be
"So there's not even beer!

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:13.152 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you're allowed
one soft drink after the show.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.120 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But you really do.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, truly, like,
we'll have a drink --

00:04:16.289 --> 00:04:19.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll have, like,
one beer in a hallway

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:23.563
where you're shouting down the
hallway to a fellow cast member.

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:28.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's, like, the closes
we've had to a party.

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:28.568 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sounds great.

00:04:28.568 --> 00:04:30.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So this is the year
to sign up, guys!

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:34.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you're looking to join,
sign up.

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.309 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I'm really selling it.

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:38.611 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And it's a dream job.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:42.181 size:84% position:42%
Everyone's on the verge
of a mental breakdown,

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:45.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you can't drink anymor
at work.

00:04:45.485 --> 00:04:47.320 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Sorry.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:49.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We did --
You know, we obviously --

00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:54.527
To be in the building, you know,
you and I get tested every day

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:55.628 line:92%
And we took advantage of that.

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:58.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm happy to say
that two weeks ago,

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:00.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
